{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"Four participants exhibited frequent episodes of freezing of gait, predominantly whilst turning.\",\n    \"Two participants showed “complete akinesia” (E2 and P3), while the other two participants exhibited “leg trembling with little effective forward motion” (E3) or “shuffling steps with minimal forward movement” (P1).\",\n    \"We asked a neurologist expert in movement disorders (A.Z.) to define these periods based on video recordings.\",\n    \"To capture the precise time windows during which both feet were “glued to the floor” 28, we combined these visually-defined periods with analyses of accelerometer data from sensors attached to the shoes of the participants.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"We exploited this platform in 18 patients with Parkinson’s disease, which allowed us to demonstrate that the subthalamic nucleus encodes the initiation, termination, and vigor of leg muscle activation.\",\n    \"We conceived a neurorobotic platform that emulated the key components of walking under well-controlled conditions, thus allowing us to isolate and quantify the encoding of lower-limb movements in the STN.\",\n    \"Participants were secured in an instrumented dynamometric chair that enabled the concomitant recordings of leg kinematics, force, electromyographic activity, and bilateral STN LFP.\",\n    \"Patients were comfortably sitting on an instrumented isokinetic machine (HUMAC NORM, CSMI, USA).\",\n    \"We translated this understanding into a machine-learning framework that decoded muscle activation, walking states, locomotor vigor, and freezing of gait.\",\n    \"Four participants exhibited frequent episodes of freezing of gait, predominantly whilst turning.\",\n    \"Kinematic detection of feet “glued to the ground”: Within the periods identified by the neurologist, we computed the times in which the feet of patients were “glued to the ground” using inertial sensors attached to the shoes of the participants.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法部分有依据。原文明确报告有4名患者出现频繁的步态冻结，而且主要发生在转弯过程中；其中包括完全运动不能、腿部颤抖但缺乏有效前进运动、拖步等不同表现。冻结时段由运动障碍专家根据视频判定，并结合鞋部惯性传感器确认双脚均未移动。因此，论文确实支持4名患者实际发生过FOG，不能认为这4人的实际冻结证据不存在。但必须区分整个研究与FOG子组：论文整体是更广泛的STN步态编码研究，摘要报告使用神经机器人平台研究了18名帕金森病患者，研究内容包括单关节腿部肌肉激活、步行状态、运动活力及FOG解码等。4人是出现频繁FOG的子组，并不是整个研究的全部参与者。因此，如果Y将整个研究说成仅有4名患者参与的转弯冻结研究，便缺少重要的研究范围限定；如果其意思是FOG分析涉及4名实际发生冻结的患者，则有原文支持。指控者对研究整体设计的描述基本正确，但其进一步声称论文不能支持4人实际冻结的证据，与原文明确记载的观察结果不符。因此，两项均判定为partly。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "2cfd8267-506a-4535-af49-bf34c56daabd", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T104919828325Z", "elapsed_seconds": 51.406, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T10:50:11.246506+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "f63b9f7e0fd89aec0f3e08fa2720a06e185a8d758ab2bdbca30db5916d02e64f", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T104919828325Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "c4f1840450eaba3c03267046f41f09d617ccdb925faa2548be8d88dfac938603"}}}
